eic770x: call the Keystone SM init from final_init

The Keystone security monitor is linked into the firmware via the
out-of-tree platform dir (sm/plat/eswin/eic770x, see PLATFORM_DIR in
overlays/keystone/boot/keystone-sm/keystone-sm.mk); this hooks its
initialization into the vendor platform, mirroring what
sm/plat/hifive/unmatched/unmatched.c does for the fu740.

Generated against eswincomputing/opensbi opensbi-1.3-EIC7X
@ f2656b169a250ca9c37253d05105f6c7dac699ca.

--- a/platform/eswin/eic770x/platform.c
+++ b/platform/eswin/eic770x/platform.c
@@ -362,10 +362,18 @@
 	return 0;
 }

+/* Keystone security monitor entry, provided by the out-of-tree platform
+ * directory (sm/plat/eswin/eic770x, wired up via PLATFORM_DIR). */
+void sm_init(bool cold_boot);
+
 static int eic770x_final_init(bool cold_boot)
 {
 	void *fdt;

+	/* sm_init() must run on every hart, so call it before the
+	 * warm-boot early return below. */
+	sm_init(cold_boot);
+
 	if (!cold_boot)
 		return 0;
